WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.400
I know for certain

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.760
that something is wrong
with that individual

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.280
and that person
will do it again

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.680
and possibly even escalate
and move on to people.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.640
So, my name
is Deanna Thompson

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.680
and you may know me
as Baudi Moovan

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.920
from Netflix's
Don't F**k with Cats.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.320
For people like me,
you wanna figure things out,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.720
you can't
just let things go.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.520
You become almost obsessed.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.320
Where it becomes like
a living and breathing thing

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.240
that you need
to get answers for.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.640
So you have to be like
really careful

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.040
not to get too attached.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.320
You also have to be
really careful

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.600
not to like accuse people
publicly.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.120
Like,
that's really dangerous.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.960
You can't start throwing

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.360
accusations out
against people

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.280
because you don't know

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.560
who's at the other end
of the keyboard

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.280
and you don't know
their mental state.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.840
We do everything
like super private.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.520
We don't post public
information

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.520
unless the person
has basically

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.800
been convicted
at that point.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.640
We don't really
do that at all

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.600
because you just
have to be so careful.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.720
We witnessed it first hand.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.480
I've experienced
my own danger

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.120
with being a web sleuth

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.240
and even though
it was nothing,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.680
it scared
the crap out of me.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.680
And the danger would come in

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.440
a couple of different ways,
I think.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.320
One is, the person or thing
that you're investigating

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.720
finds out that
you're investigating them.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.040
And then they start
investigating you.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.360
So like,
the tables are turned now

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.960
and everything
is now focused on you.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.960
And that's a dangerous thing

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.720
because the people that are
doing these crimes,

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.680
most of the time,
they want attention.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.760
And what better attention
to be like

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.240
"I'm killing these kittens…

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.160
how great would it be
if I killed the person

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.720
that's investigating me
killing these kittens.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.280
I'll get a lot of press
for that."

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.920
But then another thing
that's dangerous

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.240
is getting
too invested in it.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.000
You know, there's a quote
that Luka often sent to me.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.080
Luka is the person
that we were looking at,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.160
that was in the documentary
Don't F**k with Cats.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.120
And I don't remember
the exact quote

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.840
and I'm sure you guys
can edit this

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.200
and look it up and put it on
the screen or something,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.160
but it's the abyss quote
by Nietzsche,

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.520
it's the, you know "If you
stare too long at the abyss,

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.000
the abyss
stares back at you."

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.080
So he was like, recognising

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.960
that I was getting
too invested in finding him.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.440
And would often tag me on
like a 4chan or 7chan post

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.960
and be like "Baudi Moovan,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.440
the longer you stare
at the abyss,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.840
the abyss stares
back at you."

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.800
And every time that happened

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.640
I would be like
fuck he's right.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.960
I need to step away
for like a couple of day.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.640
So that's another danger

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.000
that any web sleuth
can get into.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.000
It's that they're just
so invested

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.280
in finding this person

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.040
that they lose all sense
of reality around them.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.040
That's a dangerous
thing to do

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.800
and your mental health
is too important to do that.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.680
I've had to go to therapy…

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.840
because of this work.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.680
And there's a lot of guilt
that comes with this work

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.680
because you want to be able
to prevent the next one,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.080
but then
the next one happens

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.440
because you didn't find out
the information in time.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.480
And there's also
a lot of like:

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.680
'Oh god, humanity is so
gross', you know.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.880
Like we are so gross,
why are we doing this?

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.560
So, I had to go to therapy

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.000
and it's out
of my own pocket.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:45.880
I have to pay for this.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.040
So it's not like I have

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.880
a professional
network to rely on,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.320
you know, like people in
law-enforcement would.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.840
The first thing
I would tell the people

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.280
that are interested
in web sleuthing

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.360
is you can't be emotional.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.000
So, if you're
an emotional person

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.160
this is not gonna be…

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.720
a good area
for you to go down.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.280
When you're
an emotional person,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.200
I'm an emotional person
so I know this,

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.840
when you're
an emotional person,

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.040
your anger and your rage

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.120
over the things
that you're investigating

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.040
sometimes
cloud your judgement.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.600
So I've learnt to kind of…

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.280
and just look at the facts.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:31.840
D'you know what I mean?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.600
And the more
you look at the facts,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:35.960
the more you get enraged

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.280
and the more
you have to calm down.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.560
So being an emotional person
is a bad thing.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.680
So, if you're
an emotional person

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.960
you really have to learn how
to tame your emotions.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.280
You don't wanna add
to the noise.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.760
The second thing I would do

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.840
is go join the web sleuth's
website and just observe.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.640
Don't participate,
just observe.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.360
I learned so much
by just watching.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.840
Sometimes just watching

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.280
you'll get more knowledge
than actually participating.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.040
So you don't always
have to have a voice,

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.480
you just sometimes
have to listen.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.240
The third thing I would
tell somebody is

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.120
don't be afraid
of technology.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.480
Technology is sometimes
this big, scary Org

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.800
that people are like afraid
to like look in,

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.680
like, how do I figure out

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.240
where this email
actually came from?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.120
People are afraid to like,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.920
use tools to figure out,
you know,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.480
those answers
and I would say

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.240
don't be afraid
of technology.

